          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "status",
            "text"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "status": {
              "const": "available"
            },
            "text": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "maxLength": 512
            }
          }
        },
        "requestedGuarantees": {
          "const": [
            "live_managed_attempt",
            "selected_route_revision",
            "normalized_request_digest",
            "transport_request_digest",
            "secret_operation_digest",
            "explicit_route_consent",
            "budget_bound",
            "one_use",
            "no_fallback"
          ]
        },
        "guaranteeAssessment": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "status",
            "residual"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "status": {
              "const": "assessed"
            },
            "residual": {
              "const": []
            }
          }
        },
        "runID": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/id"
        },
        "sessionID": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/id"
        },
        "noResponse": {
          "const": "deny_and_expire"
        },
        "allowEnabled": {
          "const": true
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "$comment": "HostKernel prepares a per-request Guard challenge bound to exact route, request, Attempt and budget. That challenge and its approved one-use lease are the provider inference consent proof. Route/request/settlement projections never accept or echo caller-supplied consent or Guard authority. Each SDK step-finish settles its immutable persisted MessageV2 snapshot; responseDigest uses horizoncode.managed-provider-response-step.v2 and includes the exact stepFinishIndex. A later SDK step creates a new monotonically sequenced provider request. Completion is allowed only from the ordered settled dispatches and final assistant snapshot, with no unresolved/in-flight request or Attempt effects. A Core restart recovers pins only through inspect_settlement, never by recomputing pins from transcript text."
}
